NOTES=Step 1 done+verified. Step 2: standalone cwasm render loop works. ORIENTATION still open. Findings: (a) shim setDisplayProjection(ROTATION_0) makes the display portrait 1440x2880 and sticks. (b) the panel forces a 90-deg transform hint -> EGL surface is 2880x1440 landscape regardless of createSurface/setBuffersGeometry. (c) render-rotate via a base matrix in SkiaRenderer (canvas_impl.rs from_native_window, WART_ORIENT env selects 4 corner-exact transforms; begin_frame/reset_matrix apply base; surface-width/height report logical) — TESTED all 4 on device: WART_ORIENT 0/1 rotate +-90 deg, 2/3 mirrored; NONE upright. Conclusion: a base-matrix rotation cannot fix it. PROPER FIX = the Android pre-rotation contract: query the Surface transform hint and call ANativeWindow_setBuffersTransform(window, hint) in the shim so SurfaceFlinger inverts our pre-rotation during composition. Then pair the base-matrix direction with the hint. Alternative: clear the hint and render a true 1440x2880 portrait buffer. Render loop + all else works; orientation is the only open item. Build host a-03 (ssh harry@a-03 -i ~/.ssh/id_rsa.my). Deploy: push wart-host + libsf_surface.so + NDK libc++_shared.so + skiko-component.cwasm to /data/local/tmp; run su -c 'LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/data/local/tmp /data/local/tmp/wart-host --standalone'.
